/Title (Explanation: First, the hook checks whether a value already exists in localStorage. If it exists, JSON.parse\(\) converts it back into a JavaScript value; otherwise, initialValue is used. Whenever the value changes, useEffect\(\) saves the new value using localStorage.setItem\(\). The hook returns [value, setValue], so it can be used almost like useState.)
